{
  "title": "America's Test Kitchen imports drop ingredient group headers",
  "description": "ATK recipes are extracted from JSON-LD recipeIngredient, which lists every ingredient but omits the group headers. \
As a result, none of the 58 ATK pipeline snapshots has a section. \
Example: americastestkitchen-com_recipes-14919-san-diego-fish-tacos has groups (Pickled Red Onion, sauce, fish, …) in the page HTML but comes out as one flat list. \
The page HTML has the groups as `<div><h3 …>Pickled Red Onion</h3><span class=\"recipePrintBody_ingredient…\">…</span>…</div>` inside `recipePrintBody_ingredientList`. \
Fix: when JSON-LD has no headers, match the recipePrintBody groups to the JSON-LD lines (same order, same text modulo whitespace and ', ' spacing) and set the section from each `<h3>`. \
Expect intentional data/ diffs from make pipeline: ATK snapshots gain sections. \
Stale prod rows like 'Chipotle Sour Cream' and 'Burritos' stored as measurement-less ingredients came from older imports. \
The promote_section_headers data migration leaves them alone because they have no colon. \
Re-importing the recipe would fix them once this lands.",
